# Read by Infra/scripts/deploy.sh (parsed, never sourced).
# INCLUDE_SIGNIN_SECRETS=1 adds the four sign-in secrets (B4HUB_SECRET_KEY and
# the three B4HUB_APPLE_* values) to the serving task definition. It stays 0
# until the sign-in hub is on main: the sign-in branch flips it to 1 when it
# merges, after the owner has given those secrets values (ECS refuses to start
# a task whose secret has none).
#
# When the sign-in branch merges (its `serve` requires B4HUB_SECRET_KEY and
# B4HUB_WEBAUTHN_RP_ID), the same pull request:
#   1. sets INCLUDE_SIGNIN_SECRETS=1 below (runbook 3 done for both accounts
#      first). That adds the four secrets to the serving task, and to the
#      admin task's `hub` container (hub-admin.json.tpl's gated block, rendered
#      by admin-shell.sh), so `b4hub seed|enroll` keep working. Both admin and
#      serving containers already set B4HUB_WEBAUTHN_RP_ID.
#   2. Compose (Hub/deploy/compose): uncomment B4HUB_SECRET_KEY in .env.example
#      and pass it to `hub` from compose.yaml's environment (a secret file with
#      B4HUB_SECRET_KEY_FILE once the hub reads _FILE forms, M8e); make test.sh
#      generate one. B4HUB_WEBAUTHN_RP_ID is already required there.
#   3. Helm: uncomment the secret key in Hub/chart/b4hub/ci/kind-values.yaml
#      and have the install job (.github/scripts/chart-kind-test.sh) generate
#      the key file it points at.
INCLUDE_SIGNIN_SECRETS=0
